  GOVERNMENT_INVESTMENT_TOOLTIP_DELAYED: "International Investments are the assets that the government holds, such as stock in companies, funds and so forth. International investments provide a yearly §YReturn of Investment (ROI)§!. Usually, this rate is 6% but it can change as the game goes on. The §YROI§! is capped at a maximum of §Y[?global.roi_rate_cap|%0]§!. Most of our §YInternational Investments§! will come from using the funds in our §YTreasury§! to invest in constructing buildings in other countries.\n\nOur current §YReturn on Investment§! is [?roi_rate|%0]\nWeekly return: $[?int_investments_rate|3]b. Treasury: $[?int_investments_collected_rate|3]b. Reinvested: $[?int_investments_reinvest_rate|3]b.\n\nIf the §YInternational Investments§! reinvestment feature is enabled, reinvested funds will not be added to our weekly income.\n\n[int_reinvestment_toggled]\n[int_auto_rejection_toggled]"
