  BUREAUCRACY_EXPENSE_TOOLTIP: "Bureaucracy Spending"
  BUREAUCRACY_EXPENSE_TOOLTIP_DELAYED: "Bureaucracy spending is how much money we use to run the administration of the country. The base cost covers infrastructure and overhead, scaled by population and §YAdministration§! level. Higher administration levels also employ a larger share of the population as civil servants, whose salaries are added on top of the infrastructure cost, meaning bureau_05 states pay both the highest overhead multiplier and the largest wage bill.\n\nGDP/C impact on §YBureaucracy Spending§!: [?education_cost_gdp_multiplier_display|-%0]\nLaw, National Spirits and Tech impact on §YBureaucracy Spending§!: [?modifier@bureaucracy_cost_multiplier_modifier|-%0]\n§YInflation§! impact on §YBureaucracy Spending§!: [?inflation_rate_var|-%]\n\nGovernment Administration Workforce Fulfillment: [?bureaucracy_manpower_fulfillment|%0]"
